# LLM providers for the Generate step. Add a key here, or connect providers in the
# app under "LLM providers" (keys entered there are stored in the local database).
#
# Free tiers:
# Gemini:  https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA:  https://build.nvidia.com  (API key from any model page)
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
#
# Any built-in preset is enabled by its <NAME>_API_KEY:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=  GROQ_API_KEY=  MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=  TOGETHER_API_KEY=  DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Local servers need no key, just a base URL:
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
#
# Every preset also reads <NAME>_BASE_URL, <NAME>_DEFAULT_MODEL (e.g. to route OpenAI
# through a proxy, or change Gemini's default model).
#
# Custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints (vLLM, LiteLLM, Azure, a company gateway), as JSON:
# LLM_PROVIDERS=[{"name": "my-vllm", "title": "My vLLM", "base_url": "http://gpu-box:8000/v1", "api_key_env": "MY_VLLM_KEY", "default_model": "qwen3-32b"}]
#   optional per entry: "key_required" (default false), "supports_reasoning" (default false), "headers": {...}
#
# Embeddings over an API (Embed → "API model") still use only the Gemini/NVIDIA keys.
